<title>GERMANY: Gehe sees 10 pct more profits from Lloyds. [CORRECTED 21:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>Gehe sees 10 pct more profits from Lloyds. [CORRECTED 21:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German pharmaceuticals wholesaler Gehe AG said on Tuesday it expected an improvement in its pre-tax profits of around 10 percent from its takeover of Britain's Lloyds Chemists Plc.</p>
<p>&quot;We see a 10 percent improvement as a result of the takeover,&quot; Gehe chairman Dieter Kaemmerer said on German television.</p>
<p>&quot;We have at the moment a pre-tax profit level of around 440 million marks and we believe we can add around 40 million (corrects from 50 million) to that (as a result of the acquisition),&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Gehe clinched a year-long fight for Lloyds on Monday after upping its bid to 684 million stg on Friday. Its first bid valued Lloyds at 584 million stg.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
